key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T20:12:26-07:00","id":1140410,"title":"","content":"There is definitely a Changeling story here! I want to know about the motley she ends up with. This was sure to trigger her chrysalis. What kind of treasure is that sword?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://imgbb.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://image.ibb.co/fzeOgQ/1172c70f3ff188688852c74c8145285c_original_2_4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> Visit my freehold for Changeling links, settings, art, and other goodies.<br /> <a href=\"https://theshepherdsfreehold.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The Shepherd's Freehold</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13648-shepherd","name":"Shepherd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T03:01:51-07:00","id":1140468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1137771-all-hail-queen-matilda?p=1140410#post1140410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is definitely a Changeling story here! I want to know about the motley she ends up with. This was sure to trigger her chrysalis. What kind of treasure is that sword?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the legendary Excalibur had given its wielder the ability to blind enemies and then sucker punch them to death... <br /> <br /> Something equally valiant, I presume?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T05:59:32-07:00","id":1140497,"title":"","content":"Perhaps it's Caliburn and it chose this newly chrysalized autumn sidhe childling to be the High Queen of the fae. The only problem is there's this guy over in Concordia named High King David who wields a sword he calls Caliburn, and although he's been a recluse for the past several years, he's not happy with this turn of events.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T07:53:45-07:00","id":1140516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1137771-all-hail-queen-matilda?p=1140497#post1140497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps it's Caliburn and it chose this newly chrysalized autumn sidhe childling to be the High Queen of the fae. The only problem is there's this guy over in Concordia named High King David who wields a sword he calls Caliburn, and although he's been a recluse for the past several years, he's not happy with this turn of events.</div> </div> </div> </div>Caliburn is the Sword in the Stone. Its Lily Saber's Noble Phantasm. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SLwANRogCxI\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SLwANRogCxI</a><br /> <br /> Excalibur is the sword given by the Lady of the Lake to Artoria later in life thus Saber proper's noble phantasm <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6b4jdV6HkIE\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6b4jdV6HkIE</a><br /> <br /> They are clearly different!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T11:05:56-07:00","id":1140561,"title":"","content":"It's a bit more complex, than that. Yes, sword from the stone and sword from the lake are different swords, indeed. <br /> <br /> But at this point we don't know, how we should be called the other one... or even which one is the &quot;other one&quot;.<br /> <br /> They are distinctly different, but both are part of the same Excalibur mythos. <br /> <br /> What I disliked about King David's story, is that Excalibur has nothing to do with Concordia or Sidhe - it's closely tied to the Britain's mythos and folklore (marking and return of Once and Future King of Britain, human king, you know - Arthur) and I never understood why was it so hard to made up new magical sword or utilize something Celtic, as an authentic High King's regalia, like Gae Bolga or something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 09-15-2017, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T12:24:33-07:00","id":1141166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1137771-all-hail-queen-matilda?p=1140497#post1140497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps it's Caliburn and it chose this newly chrysalized autumn sidhe childling to be the High Queen of the fae. The only problem is there's this guy over in Concordia named High King David who wields a sword he calls Caliburn, and although he's been a recluse for the past several years, he's not happy with this turn of events.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Holy crap, that's a cool idea! I'm totally stealing that for a game at some point!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://imgbb.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://image.ibb.co/fzeOgQ/1172c70f3ff188688852c74c8145285c_original_2_4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> Visit my freehold for Changeling links, settings, art, and other goodies.<br /> <a href=\"https://theshepherdsfreehold.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The Shepherd's Freehold</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13648-shepherd","name":"Shepherd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T19:33:54-07:00","id":1141283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1137771-all-hail-queen-matilda?p=1140561#post1140561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a bit more complex, than that. Yes, sword from the stone and sword from the lake are different swords, indeed.<br /> <br /> But at this point we don't know, how we should be called the other one... or even which one is the &quot;other one&quot;.<br /> <br /> They are distinctly different, but both are part of the same Excalibur mythos.<br /> <br /> What I disliked about King David's story, is that Excalibur has nothing to do with Concordia or Sidhe - it's closely tied to the Britain's mythos and folklore (marking and return of Once and Future King of Britain, human king, you know - Arthur) and I never understood why was it so hard to made up new magical sword or utilize something Celtic, as an authentic High King's regalia, like Gae Bolga or something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Three points: The Gae Bolga is the weapon of Cu Chulain who was not a king in any fashion. Two the Britons who became the Welsh are a Celtic people. Three Caliburn is the choser of KIngs. Excalibur is the weapon that will show up for the once and future King from the Lady of the Lake.<br /> <br /> <br /> Presumably most Kithain domains have equally awesome fate based stories of kingship(or will) too bad Vampire fucking stole Baba Yaga.. she was a great hero maker..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T14:17:25-07:00","id":1141894,"title":"","content":"Well, good for her. I just hope we don't end up with some sort of Game of Jones scenario here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12192-rabdos","name":"Rabdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12192_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T23:49:45-07:00","id":1142054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1137771-all-hail-queen-matilda?p=1141283#post1141283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Caliburn is the choser of KIngs. Excalibur is the weapon that will show up for the once and future King from the Lady of the Lake.</div> </div> </div> </div>They literally have the same name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T10:53:07-07:00","id":1142219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1137771-all-hail-queen-matilda?p=1142054#post1142054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They literally have the same name.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No they are two seperate swords in the Arthurian Mythos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T11:47:54-07:00","id":1142243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1137771-all-hail-queen-matilda?p=1142219#post1142219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No they are two seperate swords in the Arthurian Mythos.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I said earlier.<br /> <br /> I do disagree on naming. There's only one name, repeated again and again in different languages. But either they refer to both swords or one of them is nameless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T04:40:54-07:00","id":1145491,"title":"","content":"If she is moving to make good on her claim, I would suspect that <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xl77ZHXw4cY\" target=\"_blank\">Emily Henson</a> is supporting her. Nothing says &quot;power play&quot; like the infant daughter of a champion of the Undefeated publicly stealing a warrior prince's food.<br /> <br /> If not, perhaps somebody is moving to exploit her. Politics and all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T00:10:45-07:00","id":1145726,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting if you follow the threads of legend that the items that appear in the Arthurian Romances and become part of the legend are in fact the Treasures of the Four Cities. The Sword in the Stone while being &quot;Caliburn the KingMaker&quot; is fairly unimportant as its the Stone that matters, the Lias Fail which proclaims the High King by singing. The sword called Excalibur is the Sword of the Moon which cuts through any metal (this is why Excalibur is the sword of war). The Holy Grail is the Cauldron of Life that heals the sick, feeds a kingdom, restores the vitality of the land and can heal any wounds and even revive the dead... Oh and also acts as a gateway between worlds. The Spear carried by Mordred that he ruins armies with is the Spear of the Sun (actually the Spear of the Morrigan) alive and bloodthirsty which with the command Ibar will leap from its bearers hand and rip through armour and flesh with abandon, the command of Athibar crests a new trail of death as the spear returns to its owners hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}